Subject: [PATCH 0/1] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: describe the TNOC AMBA
 periphid

Hi,

the aggregator TNOC of SM8850/kaanapali, tn@111b8000, is an AMBA device
with no "arm,primecell-periphid" in its node.  The AMBA core then takes
whatever the integration leaves in the peripheral ID register; on SM8750,
whose TNOC is wired up the same way, that reads back as 0x00000000, the
coresight-tnoc amba id table (0x000f0c00/0x001f0c00, mask 0x00ffff00)
never matches, and the node is left as "deferred probe pending: (reason
unknown)".  kaanapali has the same node shape and the same missing
property, so describe the ID the driver expects.  The rest of the node
(compatible, reg size, aoss_qmp clock, in/out-ports layout) has the same
shape as SM8750; only the port list differs.

Only the DTS changes here: the binding side is shared with SM8750 and
the same relaxation was posted as patch 1/4 of Jie Gan's "Fix the
TraceNoC probe issue on QCOM platform"

  <20261118-fix-tracenoc-probe-v1-1-0298dc5f05ac@oss.qualcomm.com>

(qcom,coresight-tnoc: allow arm,primecell-periphid), and as patch 1/2 of
the SM8750 series

  <20261127113158.932414-2-xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>

Without such a change qcom,coresight-tnoc.yaml still has
additionalProperties: false and dtbs_check rejects the new property.

Note for the maintainers: this patch is the same change as patch 2/4 of
that series, which is already under review, so please treat this one as
superseded unless the platform-bus approach taken in "Fix traceNoC probe
issue on multiple QCOM platforms" is dropped instead.

Testing: no kaanapali hardware here, so the check is limited to the
bindings side.  With the binding patch applied, dtbs_check on
kaanapali-mtp.dtb and kaanapali-qrd.dtb is silent; without it, both
report "'arm,primecell-periphid' does not match any of the regexes" for
tn@111b8000, which is the same diagnostic SM8750 produced before its
fix.  dt_binding_check of the yaml passes and checkpatch --strict is
clean.  The runtime half of the argument - AMBA_ID reads 0, the driver
never matches, and adding the property makes the device bind - was
verified on SM8750 hardware (0 of 28 CoreSight AMBA devices unbound
afterwards).

